Accuracy
--------

Each kernel documents the error bound of its SLEEF accuracy tier: `u05` = 0.5
ULP, `u10` = 1.0 ULP, `u15` = 1.5 ULP, `u35` = 3.5 ULP. The bounds are asserted by
the ported upstream test suites, which compare every result against MPFR.

The vector kernels always use the target-feature-independent (split) double-double
formulation, so results do not depend on whether the build happened to enable FMA.
